<title>USA: St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Friday, barrows and gilts were steady. Top $58.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Recent sharp upturns in prices and hogs moving here early in the week. Sunshine with drying conditions and farmers bringing hogs to town and going back home to get in the fields.  Spring planting behind normal due to wet ground.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs	57.50-58.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs	56.00-57.00</p>
<p>    US 3-4    290-310 lbs	54.00-55.00</p>
<p>Sows - up $1.00-2.00. Top $50.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2     300-500 lbs    47.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3     500-550 lbs    48.00</p>
<p>		   550-700 lbs    49.00-50.00</p>
</text>
